Yeah, and like it moves quick. (Yeah.) It doesn't feel like it's like lagging.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:06.300
I'm blown away by their detail work, with, like, all the dust on the ground like they are–

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:09.820
Like that robot. Every step is kicking up a lot of dust and dirt and debris.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:14.140
I mean the thing that really stands out to me is how seamless they're coming in and out of the CG doubles of the guy,

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:16.440
to like the real-life version of the guy,

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:19.120
and, well, what makes that work is really good cloth simulation.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.426
Cloth simulation is tricky because,

00:10:20.426 --> 00:10:22.180
when you're when you have an animated character

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:26.620
There's a lot of, like, hidden parts where the– the body intersects with itself

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.840
So like if I have a shirt on in a CG character, and I go 
like this

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:33.460
Chances are, like, my model here and my model here on my character have slightly intersected

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:37.200
Which would make the cloth do an impossible thing where it pushes into the character

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.710
So it gets really tricky trying to do a good

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:40.270
full character cloth sims

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:41.520
where you have, you know,

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:44.155
an over jacket than a vest and a shirt and then pants and then a tie

00:10:44.155 --> 00:10:45.860
and like you have all these different layers

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.609
and it also has to like have the complexity with the amount of wrinkles

00:10:48.609 --> 00:10:51.220
Like, if I go like this on my shirt, like–

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:54.160
There's a lot of wrinkles and texture and like, detail in those wrinkles

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:54.880
you know?

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.920
Like, to do this, to model this, you've got to put a lot of polygons in my shirt.

00:10:57.923 --> 00:10:59.260
And very often what you see is like,

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:02.440
things end up just kind of ballooning out from the character a little bit and being too simplified.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:04.600
It almost looks like things are made out of felt.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.130
It's like look at how many wrinkles are in this jacket there

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:09.669
Look at the amount of wrinkles in his arms, look at the detail and the wrinkles on his jacket on the back.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.520
He has an undershirt.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.020
That's also a cloth sim underneath the suit jacket.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:15.600
His pants are a cloth sim.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:16.560
Everything is simulated.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.880
It's not just a static model.

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:22.800
